\begin{abstract} 
In this article we develop a theory for effectively transferring trilinear restriction estimates for the Schr\"odinger equation to functions in a more general resolution space adapted to the Schr\"odinger equation. As an application we provide a global theory for the quadratic NLS in three spatial dimensions in the critical Sobolev space $\dot{H}^{-\frac{1}{2}}$. 
\end{abstract}

